{"id": "live-257", "title": "Hexa Builders, LLC v. Monroe Township: Developer Challenges Retroactive Data Center Zoning Ban", "category": "zoning-land-use", "status": "pending", "date": "2026-07-06", "jurisdiction": "United States District Court, District of New Jersey", "state": "NJ", "amount": "$300 million sought in damages", "source": "live", "source_url": "https://newjerseymonitor.com/2026/08/20/nj-data-center-bans-courts/", "summary": "Hexa Builders, LLC sued Monroe Township, New Jersey after the township passed ordinances stripping data centers as a permitted use at Hexa's site and banning them township-wide, then rejected Hexa's data-center application for two previously approved warehouse buildings. The suit, removed to federal court on July 6, 2026, alleges violations of New Jersey's Municipal Land Use Law and federal equal-protection and First Amendment claims, and seeks the ban's repeal plus $300 million in damages.", "significance": "The case tests whether a municipality can retroactively strip or ban a previously permitted, capital-intensive use once a specific project is already in the approval pipeline. A plaintiff win would expose municipalities nationally that enact late-stage, project-targeted zoning changes to major damages exposure, raising the stakes of local political opposition to data center development well beyond a simple permit denial.", "judge": null, "tags": ["data-center", "zoning", "land-use", "new-jersey", "municipal-ban"]}
